{"name":"Majestic Evergreen","hex":"#7d8878","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"majestic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having qualities of splendor or royalty."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/majestic"},{"term":"evergreen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of plants, especially trees, that do not shed their leaves seasonally.","Continually fresh or self-renewing.\n Being a clause which causes an automatic renewal of a contract unless action is taken.\n Of a document, a piece of software, or a data set: kept continually up to date (as opposed to being published at regular intervals and outdated in the meantime)"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shrub or tree that does not shed its leaves or needles seasonally.","A conifer tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evergreen"}],"entries":[{"title":"Evergreen","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, an evergreen is a plant which has foliage that remains green and functional throughout the year. This contrasts with deciduous plants, which lose their foliage completely during the winter or dry season. Consisting of many different species, the unique feature of evergreen plants lends itself to various environments and purposes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Abies_alba_02.jpg/330px-Abies_alba_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evergreen","wikidata":"Q190489"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/%CE%95%CE%B8%CE%BD%CE%B9%CE%BA%CF%8C%CF%82_%CE%94%CF%81%CF%85%CE%BC%CF%8C%CF%82_%CE%A3%CE%B1%CE%BC%CE%B1%CF%81%CE%B9%CE%AC%CF%82.jpg/500px-%CE%95%CE%B8%CE%BD%CE%B9%CE%BA%CF%8C%CF%82_%CE%94%CF%81%CF%85%CE%BC%CF%8C%CF%82_%CE%A3%CE%B1%CE%BC%CE%B1%CF%81%CE%B9%CE%AC%CF%82.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/th